7. The nurse is caring for a woman who has a cyst in her breast that was found at her recent 
mammogram. The physician wants to make sure that the cyst is not malignant. Which test will be 
used to determine this? 
a. Needle aspiration with biopsy 
b. Paracentesis 
c. Thoracentesis 
d. Fiberoptic endoscopy 
ANS: A 
Needle aspirations are procedures that are used to remove fluid and tissue for testing. A biopsy 
involves removing a larger collection of cells, as in a tumor or mass, and may be used to detect 
cancer in the skin, breast, or liver. Paracentesis is drainage of fluid from the abdomen, and 
thoracentesis is drainage of fluid from the pleural cavity. Fiberoptic endoscopy allows the physician 
to see inside the upper and/or lower GI tract. 
