1. The nurse identifies which medication that has the highest potential for abuse? 
a. Methylphenidate (Ritalin)—schedule II 
b. Alprazolam (Xanax)—schedule IV 
c. Acetaminophen & codeine (Tylenol #3)—schedule III 
d. Diphenoxylate & atropine (Lomotil)—schedule V 
ANS: A 
According to the Controlled Substances Act, drugs that have the potential for abuse/dependency  
are classified as schedule I-V. Schedule I drugs have no approved medical applications in the United 
States. Schedule II drugs have high potential for abuse/dependency and have multiple restrictions 
for prescriptions. Schedule III, IV, and V have lower risks of dependency/abuse and fewer 
restrictions for prescriptions. Methylphenidate has the highest risk of abuse in this selection. 
