levels. High-flow oxygen may lead to respiratory suppression caused by loss of the patient‘s drive to 
breathe. The nurse should reduce the oxygen flow rate until the patient‘s pulse oximetry is more 
than 90% and educate the patient about oxygen therapy for COPD. 
