Only the inner cannula of the tracheostomy is removed for cleaning. The outer cannul a stays in  
the trachea to maintain airway patency. Clean gloves are applied before the soiled dress ing is  
removed. Normal sterile saline is used to remove secretions that have built u p on the inner  
cannula and also is used to clean the patient‘s skin as needed. 
